IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch4-fourth-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch4.l4: tests for the Fourth Schedule.  Expected values are written from the text of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 5830-5954) beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Fourth Schedule`

-- A decision with the facts the Schedule turns on; the other fields of Decision are placeholders no rule here reads.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      about IS A `Subject of an order or application`
      way IS A `Way an order went`
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
      afterTrial IS A BOOLEAN
      agreedFinal IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decision
`sch 4 test: a decision` MEANS
    Decision WITH
        `made by` IS court
        `in the exercise of` IS jurisdiction
        `nature of the proceeding` IS `a civil proceeding`
        `subject of the case` IS `any other civil matter`
        `the order` IS (Order OF about, way)
        `made after the trial of an action` IS afterTrial
        `made by consent of the parties` IS consent
        `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
        `date made` IS Date 1 7 2024
        `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
        `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
        `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS agreedFinal

-- The eleven facts in the order of the record: a Judge made the order; limitation expired; name or capacity; new cause of action; s 23 FJA;
-- proves fraud; proves natural-justice breach; agreement covers only part; appeal is against that part; expedited procedure; request refused.
GIVEN judge IS A BOOLEAN, limitation IS A BOOLEAN, nameOrCapacity IS A BOOLEAN, newCause IS A BOOLEAN, s23 IS A BOOLEAN
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN, naturalJustice IS A BOOLEAN, partOnly IS A BOOLEAN, thatPart IS A BOOLEAN, expedited IS A BOOLEAN, refusedRequest IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
`sch 4 test: facts` MEANS
    `sch 4 facts about the decision` WITH
        `a Judge made the order` IS judge
        `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired` IS limitation
        `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues` IS nameOrCapacity
        `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action` IS newCause
        `the decision involves the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014` IS s23
        `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS fraud
        `the party seeking to appeal proves a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice` IS naturalJustice
        `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision` IS partOnly
        `the appeal is against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to` IS thatPart
        `the action was ordered, with the consent of all the parties, to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals` IS expedited
        `the order refused a request, made with the consent of all the parties, for the expedited procedure` IS refusedRequest

`sch 4 test: no special facts` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: a Judge made the order` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, name or capacity corrected` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, new cause of action` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, neither limb (ii) fact` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, no limitation, new cause of action` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: proves fraud` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: proves natural justice breach` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`sch 4 test: expedited procedure, no Judge` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`sch 4 test: Judge, request for expedited procedure refused` MEANS `sch 4 test: facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

`sch 4 test: GD order by consent` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `recording a judgment or order made by consent` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: SICC order by consent` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` `recording a judgment or order made by consent` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: DC order by consent` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `recording a judgment or order made by consent` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD gave further and better particulars` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `further and better particulars` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused further and better particulars` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `further and better particulars` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD order on further and better particulars that is neither` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `further and better particulars` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `amending a pleading` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused permission to amend` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `amending a pleading` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused security for costs` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `security for costs` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD gave security for costs` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `security for costs` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD gave interrogatories` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` interrogatories `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused interrogatories` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` interrogatories refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `discovery or inspection of documents` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: FD appellate decision` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `appellate jurisdiction` `recording a judgment or order made by consent` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: FD original decision by consent` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `original jurisdiction` `recording a judgment or order made by consent` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD agreed final` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `discovery or inspection of documents` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`sch 4 test: DC agreed final` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `discovery or inspection of documents` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`sch 4 test: GD summary judgment` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `summary judgment` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused summary judgment` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `summary judgment` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD jurisdiction order` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `whether the court has jurisdiction or should exercise it` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused to set aside a default judgment` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `setting aside a default judgment` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD set aside a default judgment` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `setting aside a default judgment` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD struck out the action` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `striking out an action or a matter commenced by originating process` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD dismissed the action on striking out a pleading` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `dismissing an action, or entering judgment, upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD stayed proceedings` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a stay of proceedings` `granted unconditionally` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD refused a stay` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a stay of proceedings` refused FALSE FALSE FALSE
`sch 4 test: GD judgment after trial` MEANS `sch 4 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `another order or application` `granted unconditionally` FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 2 ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` `sch 4 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Family Division decision that does not involve the s 23 jurisdiction: para 2 does not speak to it
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` `sch 4 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` `sch 4 test: FD original decision by consent` `sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` `sch 4 test: GD order by consent` `sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 1(b): made by consent ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` `sch 4 test: GD order by consent`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1(h): further and better particulars ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: GD gave further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: GD refused further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- made by the Registrar, not a Judge
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: GD gave further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: GD order on further and better particulars that is neither` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` `sch 4 test: GD gave interrogatories` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1(i): permission to amend, except if (i) and (ii) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the exception: after limitation AND the amendment corrects a name or capacity
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, name or capacity corrected`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the exception: after limitation AND the effect is a new cause of action
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, new cause of action`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- limitation expired but neither (ii) fact: the exception needs both (i) and (ii), so the limb holds
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, neither limb (ii) fact`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (ii) fact but limitation not expired: the exception needs both, so the limb holds
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, no limitation, new cause of action`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- refusing permission is not "giving permission"
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1(j): refusing security for costs ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(j) a Judge refuses security for costs` `sch 4 test: GD refused security for costs` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(j) a Judge refuses security for costs` `sch 4 test: GD gave security for costs` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(j) a Judge refuses security for costs` `sch 4 test: GD refused security for costs` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1(k): interrogatories ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(k) a Judge gives or refuses interrogatories` `sch 4 test: GD gave interrogatories` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(k) a Judge gives or refuses interrogatories` `sch 4 test: GD refused interrogatories` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1(k) a Judge gives or refuses interrogatories` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 1 as a whole ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: GD order by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Singapore International Commercial Court is read as within "General Division" through s 18C
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: SICC order by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: GD gave interrogatories` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Subject to paragraph 2": a Family Division appellate decision under s 23 is out even if made by consent
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a Family Division original decision by consent: the Schedule does not say whether the Family Division is part of the General Division
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: FD original decision by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a District Court decision is not within a Schedule headed "Decisions of General Division"
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `sch 4 test: DC order by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 3(2)(a): when the agreement was made ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) before the decision was made`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) after the decision was made`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) at the same time as the decision`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 3(2)(b): an agreement about part of a decision ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` `sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 3(1): agreed in writing that the decision is final ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the party seeking to appeal proves (a) fraud or illegality; or (b) a fundamental breach of natural justice"
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: proves fraud`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: proves natural justice breach`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no agreement in writing
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the agreement covers only part of the decision and the appeal is against another part
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against another part`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: agreement covers part only, appeal is against that part`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a decision of the District Court is outside a paragraph about "a decision of the General Division"
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` `sch 4 test: DC agreed final` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 4(1)(a) to (i): the decisions that stay appealable ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(a) the order is that the Court has no jurisdiction or should not exercise it` `sch 4 test: GD jurisdiction order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(a) the order is that the Court has no jurisdiction or should not exercise it` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(b) the order is for summary judgment` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order refusing summary judgment is not "an order for summary judgment"
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(b) the order is for summary judgment` `sch 4 test: GD refused summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(c) the order refuses to set aside a default judgment` `sch 4 test: GD refused to set aside a default judgment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(c) the order refuses to set aside a default judgment` `sch 4 test: GD set aside a default judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(d) the order is for the striking out of the action` `sch 4 test: GD struck out the action`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(d) the order is for the striking out of the action` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(e) the order dismisses the action or enters judgment upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` `sch 4 test: GD dismissed the action on striking out a pleading`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(e) the order dismisses the action or enters judgment upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` `sch 4 test: GD struck out the action`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f): giving OR refusing permission to amend, where (i) and (ii)
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, name or capacity corrected`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` `sch 4 test: GD refused permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, new cause of action`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, limitation expired, neither limb (ii) fact`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` `sch 4 test: GD gave permission to amend` `sch 4 test: Judge, no limitation, new cause of action`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(g) the order gives security for costs` `sch 4 test: GD gave security for costs`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(g) the order gives security for costs` `sch 4 test: GD refused security for costs`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(h) the order is for a stay of proceedings` `sch 4 test: GD stayed proceedings`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(h) the order is for a stay of proceedings` `sch 4 test: GD refused a stay`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(i) the decision is a judgment given after the trial of an action` `sch 4 test: GD judgment after trial`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1)(i) the decision is a judgment given after the trial of an action` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) the decision is one of those that remain appealable` `sch 4 test: GD stayed proceedings` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) the decision is one of those that remain appealable` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- paragraph 4(1): the expedited procedure ----
-- a decision of a Judge in an expedited action that is not one of the nine: no appeal
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one of the nine: the exception takes it out of the bar
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD summary judgment` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD stayed proceedings` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD judgment after trial` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an expedited action
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expedited action but the decision is not a Judge's
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: expedited procedure, no Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: DC agreed final` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- paragraph 4(2): refusing a request for the expedited procedure ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(2) an appeal cannot be brought against an order refusing the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: Judge, request for expedited procedure refused`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(2) an appeal cannot be brought against an order refusing the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 para 4(2) an appeal cannot be brought against an order refusing the expedited procedure` `sch 4 test: DC agreed final` `sch 4 test: Judge, request for expedited procedure refused`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the Schedule as a whole (seam 4) ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD order by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: Judge, expedited procedure`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: Judge, request for expedited procedure refused`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- agreed final but the appellant proves fraud: para 3(1) lets the appeal be brought, and no other paragraph lists the decision
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD agreed final` `sch 4 test: proves fraud`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision no paragraph lists
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: GD gave discovery` `sch 4 test: a Judge made the order`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Family Division appellate decision under s 23: paragraph 2 takes it out of paragraph 1
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: FD appellate decision` `sch 4 test: Family Division, s 23 appellate jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- outside the Schedule's scope
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: DC order by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` `sch 4 test: FD original decision by consent` `sch 4 test: no special facts`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the helpers ----
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 4 the order gave` `granted unconditionally`
#ASSERT `sch 4 the order gave` `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 4 the order gave` refused)
#ASSERT `sch 4 the order gave or refused` refused
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 4 the order gave or refused` `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal`)
